      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b365393bda79-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "If a 20 m long rope is cut into pieces of 1.6 m each, what percentage of the rope will be left over?",
      "questionHtml": "If a 20 m long rope is cut into pieces of 1.6 m each, what percentage of the rope will be left over?<span style=\"display: none;\">&nbsp;</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "20%",
          "html": "20%"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "8%",
          "html": "8%"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4%",
          "html": "4%"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "10%",
          "html": "10%"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /> <u style=\"font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700; display: inline !important;\">Shortcut Trick</u></span>\n<p>Total pieces = 20 ÷ 1.6 = 12.5 pieces.</p>\n<p>Full pieces cut = 12. Remainder = 0.5 pieces.</p>\n<p>Length of leftover = 0.5 × 1.6 = 0.8 m.</p>\n<p>Leftover percentage = (0.8 ÷ 20) × 100 = 4%.</p>\n<p>In decimal form, 4% is expressed as 0.04.</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct option is C.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Alternate Method</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p>Given: Total length = 20 m, Piece length = 1.6 m.</p>\n<p>Formula used: Remainder = Total length − (Number of whole pieces × Length of one piece)</p>\n<svg width=\"420\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"display:block;margin:12px 0;background:#ffffff;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid #cccccc;\">\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"80\" width=\"340\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#ddeeff\" stroke=\"#2255cc\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"366\" y=\"80\" width=\"14\" height=\"30\" fill=\"#fff0cc\" stroke=\"#cc5500\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n  <line x1=\"67\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"67\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#cc0000\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"94\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"94\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#cc0000\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"366\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"366\" y2=\"110\" stroke=\"#cc0000\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,3\"/>\n  <text x=\"40\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#2255cc\" font-size=\"12\">0 m</text>\n  <text x=\"360\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#2255cc\" font-size=\"12\">19.2 m</text>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"70\" fill=\"#2255cc\" font-size=\"12\">20 m</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#222222\" font-size=\"12\">12 Full Pieces (1.6 m each)</text>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"140\" fill=\"#cc5500\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"12\">Leftover = 0.8 m</text>\n  <text x=\"160\" y=\"175\" fill=\"#2255cc\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"14\">Total Rope Length = 20 m</text>\n</svg>\n<p>⇒ Number of complete pieces = 20 ÷ 1.6 = 12.5</p>\n<p>⇒ Total pieces = 12 (since only whole pieces are cut)</p>\n<p>⇒ Length of 12 pieces = 12 × 1.6 = 19.2 m</p>\n<p>⇒ Length of leftover rope = 20 − 19.2 = 0.8 m</p>\n<p>⇒ Percentage of leftover = (Leftover ÷ Total Length) × 100</p>\n<p>⇒ Percentage = (0.8 ÷ 20) × 100 = 4%</p>\n<p>⇒ Expressed in options as a decimal: 4/100 = 0.04</p>\n<p><strong>∴ The correct option is C.</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Percentage to Decimal</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">To convert a percentage into a decimal, divide the number by 100. Example: x% = x/100.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Division and Remainder</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">Dividend = (Divisor × Quotient) + Remainder. Here, 20 = (1.6 × 12) + 0.8.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 2px 0;font-weight:700;color:#222222;\">Percentage Change</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#444444;\">Percentage change = (Change ÷ Original Value) × 100. This is used to find leftovers or profit/loss ratios.</p>",
      "images": [
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/shortcut-trick-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/alternate-methord-image.png",
        "//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b365393bda79-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "Express \\(4.\\overline{142}\\) in the form \\(\\frac{p}{q}\\) , where p and q are integers and q &ne; 0.",
      "questionHtml": "Express&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(4.\\overline{142}\\)</span> in the form <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{p}{q}\\)</span>, where p and q are integers and q&nbsp;&ne; 0.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{4136}{999}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4136}{999}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{4140}{999}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4140}{999}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{4142}{999}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4142}{999}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "\\(\\frac{4138}{999}\\)",
          "html": "<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4138}{999}\\)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Let, x = <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(4.142142\\)</span>.................. (1)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">multiply eq (1) by 1000, and we get   ( because there are three digits that have bar means are repeating)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">1000x = 4142.142142....... (2)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now subtract eq (1) by eq (2)</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">1000x - x = 4142.142142 - 4.142142, 999x = 4138, x = <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{4138}{999}\\)</span></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b365393bda79-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "0.12112111211112 ______ is a number, which is?",
      "questionHtml": "0.12112111211112 ______ is a number, which is?&nbsp;",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Rational",
          "html": "Rational&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Irrational",
          "html": "Irrational&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Non-real",
          "html": "Non-real&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "None of these",
          "html": "None of these&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Explanation</strong> -</p>\n\n<p>The pattern seems to repeat a sequence of numbers: 121, 1211, 12111, and so on, with an additional 2 at the end.</p>\n\n<p>This type of sequence, where each segment extends by adding one more digit to the end, repeating the previous pattern, suggests an irrational number.</p>\n\n<p>Irrational numbers are decimal numbers that neither terminate nor repeat in a specific pattern.</p>\n\n<p>In this case, while there&#39;s a repeating structure within the sequence, the addition of a new digit at each step makes it non-repeating and non-terminating, fitting the definition of an irrational number.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hence Option (2) is correct.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b365393bda79-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "Let x = \\(\\frac{6}{5}\\) , then arrange the numbers 6x, \\(\\frac{37}{6}\\) , 6 - x and 5 + x in ascending order.",
      "questionHtml": "Let x =&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{6}{5}\\)</span>, then arrange the numbers 6x,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)</span>&nbsp;, 6 - x and 5 + x in ascending order.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6 - x, \\(\\frac{37}{6}\\) , 5 + x, 6x",
          "html": "6 - x,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)</span>, 5 + x, 6x"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "6 - x, 5 + x, 6x, \\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)",
          "html": "6 - x, 5 + x, 6x,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "6 - x, 5 + x, \\(\\frac{37}{6}\\) , 6x",
          "html": "6 - x, 5 + x,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)</span>, 6x"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "6 - x, \\(\\frac{37}{6}\\) , 6x, 5 + x",
          "html": "6 - x,&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)</span>, 6x, 5 + x"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>x = 6/5</p>\n\n<p>Numbers: 6x, 37/6, 6 - x, 5 + x</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>6x = 6 &times; (6/5) = 36/5 = 7.2</p>\n\n<p>6 - x = 6 - (6/5) = (30/5) - (6/5) = 24/5 = 4.8</p>\n\n<p>5 + x = 5 + (6/5) = (25/5) + (6/5) = 31/5 = 6.2</p>\n\n<p>37/6 = 6.1666...</p>\n\n<p>The numbers are in ascending order:</p>\n\n<p>4.8 &lt; 6.1666... &lt; 6.2 &lt; 7.2</p>\n\n<p>24/5 &lt; 37/6 &lt; 31/5 &lt; 36/5</p>\n\n<p>6 - x &lt; 37/6 &lt; 5 + x &lt; 6x</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The ascending order is: 6 - x, 37/6, 5 + x, 6x.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "b365393bda79-q8",
